1	/**
2	 * Port of `whoosh.analysis.filters`.
3	 *
4	 * A filter takes the token stream produced by a tokenizer (or by the previous
5	 * filter) and yields a transformed stream. Every filter here is a generator, so
6	 * the whole analysis chain stays lazy: nothing is computed until the consumer
7	 * pulls a token.
8	 *
9	 * Filters MUTATE the token they were handed and re-yield it, exactly as Whoosh
10	 * does. In Whoosh that works because the tokenizer recycles one Token object;
11	 * here it works because our tokenizers hand out a fresh Token per token (see
12	 * ./token.mjs), which makes the stream safe to materialize as well.
13	 */
