136	/**
137	 * Port of `whoosh.analysis.filters.StopFilter`.
138	 *
139	 * A token is removed when ANY of these holds:
140	 *   - its length (in code points) is < minsize, or
141	 *   - maxsize is set and its length is > maxsize, or
142	 *   - its text is in the stop list.
143	 *
144	 * The length test is a pure character-length test and is completely independent
145	 * of the stop list, so the default minsize=2 makes single letters and single
146	 * digits unsearchable in a default TEXT field ("Vitamin C", "Plan B",
147	 * "Section 5" all lose that token).
148	 *
149	 * When `removestops` is false on the token (query-side "keep the holes"
150	 * behaviour), the token is FLAGGED via `token.stopped = true` and still yielded
151	 * instead of being dropped.
152	 *
153	 * `renumber` (default true) closes the positional gaps left by removed tokens,
154	 * so a phrase query spanning a removed stop word behaves as if the stop word had
155	 * never been there. Exactly as in Whoosh, the first surviving token keeps its
